30. Architecture Decision Rules

Choose MongoDB

for operational document data and geospatial operational queries.

Choose S3

for large files and scientific artifacts.

Choose Redis

for transient/cache state.

Choose Celery

for asynchronous Python jobs.

Choose NetworkX first

for initial network analysis.

Add Kafka later

only when event throughput/architecture requires it.

Add Neo4j later

only if graph workload proves the need.

Add Kubernetes later

only if scale/operations justify it.

Add GPU infrastructure

only for measured ML workload requirements.

